WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.460
We learnt that objects are visible because of the

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.500
light getting reflected from their surfaces.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.700
This reflected light enters our eyes

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.320
and we see that object.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.360
What happens inside the human eye

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:19.660
when light rays enter it?

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:23.000
What is it that helps us see the things around us?

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.660
The human eye is roughly spherical in shape.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.860
What we’re going to do in this video

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.880
is understand the different parts of the eye in short...

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.740
not in extreme detail.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.320
Let’s begin!

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.420
The outer layer of the eye is called the CORNEA.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.100
It is white in colour and transparent.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.520
Transparent?

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:43.140
Yes,

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:46.240
it means that it allows light to pass through it!

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:49.420
It acts like a tough front wall of the eye.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.220
What is its function?

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:54.220
It protects the interior of the eye from accidents

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.900
and also does not allow foreign particles

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.760
to enter the eye.

00:00:58.900 --> 00:00:59.400
Okay,

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:02.620
so this was all about the outer layer of the eye.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:06.100
Let’s now talk about the things present INSIDE.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:07.320
Behind the cornea

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.480
there is a dark muscular structure called the IRIS.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.420
Iris determines the colour of the eye.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.460
For instance when we say that a person has blue eyes,

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:17.140
it means

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:20.760
that the colour of the iris of person’s eye is blue.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.480
Now there is a small opening at the centre of the iris

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.660
for the light to enter.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:27.360
Do you know what it’s called?

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.580
It is called the PUPIL.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:33.320
The Iris actually acts like a shutter of a camera.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.020
It controls the amount of light entering the eye

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:37.780
by enlarging or shrinking

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.960
and thereby adjusting the size of the pupil.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:42.100
For example,

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.720
when you focus the light from the torch

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:47.420
directly into a person’s eye the iris shrinks.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.280
This is because

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.980
the intensity of light is too much for the eyes to bear!

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:53.640
The shrinking iris stops the

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:56.620
unwanted light from entering through the pupil.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.340
And when it’s dark or when there’s less light,

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:01.240
it expands allowing more light to enter

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.040
through the pupil.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.020
Ok,

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.680
what happens next?

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.560
The light that enters through the pupil

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:10.320
falls on the LENS kept behind

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.980
This lens is a CONVEX LENS.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.940
What is a convex lens?

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.960
Convex lens is a lens which is thicker at the centre

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:19.460
than the edges.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:21.420
It is a CONVERGING LENS.

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:25.200
That is, it focuses all the light at one point.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.440
In a normal regular eye this point is somewhere here,

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:31.640
on this inner boundary called RETINA.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:33.840
Why do i say a normal eye?

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:34.440
Well,

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:35.420
in a defective eye,

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.660
this point of focus may lie either in front of the retina

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:40.660
or behind the retina.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:44.080
We will talk about this defect of eye in our future videos

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.480
but first let’s go back to our normal eye

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.660
where light is focussed ON the retina.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:51.560
Retina is at the back of the eye

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.920
and marks the inner layer of the eyeball.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.180
Retina contains lots of NERVE CELLS

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.860
that sense light.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.700
The nerve cells are of two kinds namely CONES

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.480
which are sensitive to bright light

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:06.640
and RODS which are sensitive to dim light.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.680
The message or sensation is then

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:11.600
transferred to the brain along the optic nerve.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:12.300
Ok,

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.487
let’s quickly recap what we learned

00:03:14.487 --> 00:03:15.680
about the human eye.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:18.460
Human eye has a roughly spherical shape.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:20.760
The outer part of an eye called CORNEA

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:22.820
is a thick white transparent wall,

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:25.200
which protects the eye from accidents

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:28.740
and keeps the foreign particles from entering inside.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:30.020
Behind the cornea,

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:34.040
the colourful part of the eye called IRIS is present.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:37.720
It has a small opening at the centre called PUPIL.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:40.280
Iris controls the light entering through the pupil

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:43.120
by contracting and expanding.

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:45.460
Behind the pupil there is a converging lens

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:48.520
which focuses the light on retina.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.480
Retina consists of two types of nerve cells

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:53.780
namely cones and rods.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.820
They transfer the message through the optic nerve.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:59.140
That’s a lot of information to digest!

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:01.460
So we will stop here and continue to learn

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.960
more about the eye in the next lesson.

